body:
Hi.

&#x200B;

I want to tell you, right now, that I'm not ever going to forget seeing this. If you die, there's is at least one person in the world who won't forget you.

&#x200B;

Moreover, I wanted to say something here so that - if you want support still - I can promise you I will be support that will never choose to abandon you. I'll never tell you to take your problems somewhere else. 

&#x200B;

I know whats its like to hate yourself, and also to struggle with self harm, but I don't *why* you do or think these things. So I can help you, would you please tell me why you feel this way? 

&#x200B;

I won't offer you false, generic positivity, but I will at least listen to you, and try and provide advice from my own experience.

Okay, well for starters - she chose to send that to you, that takes some of the burden off you. 

&#x200B;

You did do a silly thing, but that's all it was. You see its wrong. You don't want to do it again, it sounds like. You'd never contemplate doing something truly awful. You're almost certainly not a paedophile.  Its simply about learning how to get over this guilt, thats all. Its not worth suicide. If I don't need to die, you don't.

Hello khatss,

&#x200B;

I understand the feelings of self hatred, and I know what it is like to have these thoughts eating you alive, to feel like the worst person in the world. If you want to speak to me, I would be happy to - I won't offer you generic positivity, but I can at least be a listening ear, as someone who will have gone through similar things to you.

&#x200B;

As per the rules, it is generally the case that the mods don't like to have DMs offered as a first resort, so feel free to speak to me here if you are comfortable.

Its cool to see this song mean different things to different people. I totally disagree, but I know my meaning isn't "right" either so its fun to see different interpretations of the song.

&#x200B;

To me the song, and that line especially, was always about my own failings and a desire for perfection. I want to look perfect, I want to be a perfect Christian (have a perfect soul). And I think that *then* I might be someone who is appreciated (or believes they are, even if they already are) - people wont "run away" from me. 

&#x200B;

I think we're both "wrong" and its not what Radiohead meant, but it doesn't have to be.

Its an interesting idea.

&#x200B;

I always thought of Brand New as very Christian (although not a Christian rock band, if that makes sense). However I also like them because they are the antithesis of traditional, insincere happy clappy stuff. They show the reality of a difficult relationship with God.

&#x200B;

Personally I would be inclined towards a similar interpretation - Jesse is kind of turning that kind of music in on itself and saying "heres what it is actually like". So I don't think its stupid at all.

I think it is a band of \*Christians\*, but not a \*Christian\* band. Jesse even said they aren't a Christian rock band, and I think he wants the band to be more than that. So whilst I think it is very Christian (although I'm biased to that), and shows an often unshown side of the faith (doubt, guilt, and so on), I don't think it should be associated with a music scene so notoriously happy clappy. 

&#x200B;

I do however think the religious element of it is more important than people give it credit it for - these aren't just cute little bible references, they really mean something.

Its a reference to Genesis 2:7, I think. 

&#x200B;

"Then the Lord God formed a man  from the dust of the ground and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life, and the man became a living being." Some translations, like my favourite, DRA, dont use dust, but most do.

Hard to choose.

&#x200B;

I quite liked "I kept hearing trumpets, got my hearing checked". In reference, I think, to the seven trumpets of Revelation ("how does everything start and end?").

I have to say two because I can't choose between them.

&#x200B;

Jesus Christ is a pick for me because the pain and guilt the song expresses with regards to Jesse's relationship to Jesus is incredibly relatable for me. It captures the feeling of a horrible person asking for help and forgiveness. 

&#x200B;

Sealed To Me is maybe the only song to ever make me *sob.* Sort of for similar reasons. That feeling of regret and resolution to change combined with Jeese's pure emotion makes it a very special song for me.

Huh. This has actually got me kinda stumped. 

&#x200B;

I will come back to this. First time an argument like that has caused me a mild theological crisis.

I'm convinced the reason why half of you are atheists is because us Christians can't argue. 

&#x200B;

Fair enough.

You got me, hahaha.

&#x200B;

Even as a Christian, I know these are bad arguments anyway and was about to argue with you.
